  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Lily and Pip are at the playground. Lily sits in the sand. \"Our sand is yellow,\" she says. Pip sits next to her. \"Pip, what color is the wall?\" asks Lily. \"Woof!\" says Pip. \"Yes, it is white!\" says Lily. She smiles. \"Look at the bird!\" A blue bird sits on the wall. It is small and nice.",
      "Then a bee comes. The bee is yellow and black. It flies next to Pip. Pip jumps. He runs behind Lily. \"Don't worry, Pip,\" says Lily. \"The bee is not scary.\" \"It likes flowers.\" Pip looks at Lily. \"Is the bee our friend?\"",
      "The bee flies to a pink flower. Pip looks at the bee. He is not sad now. Lily draws a bee in the sand. \"What color is the bee?\" asks Lily. \"Yellow and black!\" Pip sits in the sand, too. He sees white, blue, pink, and yellow. \"Our playground has many colors,\" says Lily. Pip says, \"Woof!\""
    ],
    "summary": "Lily and Pip play in the sand at the playground. They see a blue bird and a yellow bee, and Pip learns that the bee is not scary.",
